# Trading Desk end-user licence

This is the licence for the Trading Desk application. It repeats the terms of sale and use at
<https://futureinvoked.uk/projects/trading-desk/terms>.

## Who grants it

The provider named in the imprint at <https://futureinvoked.uk/imprint/>. Checkout is
handled by Stripe, through its Link service, as merchant of record, which manages payment, taxes
and refunds.

## What you get

- **Beginner or Pro key:** a personal, non-transferable licence to use Trading Desk on the
  computers you own, with updates for the 1.x series.
- **Beginner** covers 5 tickers across your portfolio and watchlist and the core features.
- **Pro** covers every feature and any number of tickers.
- **Upgrade:** a Beginner key can be upgraded to Pro for the difference in price.
- **Free trial:** anyone can use Trading Desk free for 10 days. After it, the desk is read-only
  until a key is added. Every record stays, and nothing is deleted.
- **No resale:** you may not share, sell or publish your key, or the application's files.

## Refunds and withdrawal

- **Refund:** if the application does not do what
  <https://futureinvoked.uk/projects/trading-desk> says, write within 30 days and you get your
  money back. A refunded key is no longer licensed.
- **EU withdrawal:** consumers in the EU can also withdraw from the purchase within 14 days of
  the day they buy, without giving a reason. Write to <futureinvoked@proton.me> and you get your
  money back.

## What it is not

Trading Desk is decision-support software. It collects public market data and your own notes,
and it lays them out. It is not investment, tax or legal advice, it recommends no security, and
it never places orders.

The AI features run through your own Claude or Codex account, under Anthropic's or OpenAI's
terms. What they write is a draft for you to check, not advice. You remain responsible for every
trade and every figure you rely on.

## As-is and liability

The software is provided as-is. To the extent the law allows, liability is limited to the price
you paid. Nothing here limits liability for intent, gross negligence, or injury to life, body or
health.

## Privacy

- **Activation:** checking a licence key sends nothing anywhere.
- **What leaves your computer:** the data sources, the AI providers and checkout each see only
  what the privacy notice at <https://futureinvoked.uk/projects/trading-desk/privacy/> lists.

## Law and seller

The seller and the applicable law are given in the imprint. Mandatory consumer protections of
your country of residence are unaffected.

## Software from others inside

The application includes software from others under its own licences: Python, the Python
packages, TradingView Lightweight Charts and, on Windows, Microsoft's WebView2 libraries. Each
one, its licence and its copyright notices are listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt, which comes
with the application.
